    # κ (KAPPA) - [SCm] REACTIVITY DECAY RATE
    # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    # Definition: κ = 0.0005 day⁻¹ = 5×10⁻⁴ day⁻¹
    #
    # Full Name: [SCm] Reactivity Decay Rate
    # Quantifies rate at which [SCm]'s reactivity decays over time.
    #
    # Characteristic Decay Time:
    #   τ = 1/κ = 2,000 days ≈ 5.48 years
    #   Time for reactivity to decay to 1/e ≈ 0.368 of initial value.
    #
    # CRITICAL DISTINCTION FROM γ (GAMMA):
    # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    #   κ = 0.0005 day⁻¹ → τ = 2,000 days ≈ 5.5 years ([SCm] reactivity)
    #   γ = 0.00005 day⁻¹ → τ = 20,000 days ≈ 55 years (magnetism reciprocation)
    #
    #   κ is 10× LARGER than γ → 10× FASTER decay!
    #   - κ controls E_react decay (reactor efficiency)
    #   - γ controls Um time factor (magnetic field evolution)
    #
    # Role in E_react:
    # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    #   E_react = (ρ_vac,[SCm] × v_SCm²) / ρ_vac,A × e^(-κt)
    #   Simplified: E_react = 10⁴⁶ × e^(-0.0005t)
    #
    # Decay Profile:
    # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    #   t = 0:      E_react = 10⁴⁶ (100%)
    #   t = 1000d:  E_react ≈ 6.07×10⁴⁵ (60.7%)
    #   t = 2000d:  E_react ≈ 3.68×10⁴⁵ (36.8%, 1/e)
    #   t = 4000d:  E_react ≈ 1.35×10⁴⁵ (13.5%)
    #
    # Physical Interpretation:
    # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    #   [SCm] is massless, extra-universal material that reacts with [UA].
    #   κ quantifies how quickly [SCm]'s ability to interact decays over time.
    #   The ~5.5-year timescale is relevant for:
    #     - Nebular dynamics and magnetic field generation
    #     - Star formation collapse dynamics and jet formation
    #     - Quasar jet sustained energy transfer
    #
    # Scales These Energy Terms (via E_react):
    # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    #   • Um (Universal Magnetism): Magnetic string energy density
    #   • Ubi (Universal Buoyancy): Buoyancy from gravity-vacuum interaction
    #   • Ui (Universal Inertia): Inertial energy from [SCm]/[UA] interaction
    #   • Ug2, Ug3, Ug4 (Universal Gravity): Gravitational components
    #
